{
  "id": "geo-lines",
  "chapterNumber": "2",
  "title": {
    "en": "Lines &amp; Angles",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "When a <strong>transversal</strong> cuts two parallel lines, eight angles appear — but only two distinct measures. Knowing which pairs are equal and which are supplementary unlocks most angle-chase problems.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Parallel lines &amp; a transversal",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Corresponding</strong> angles are equal; <strong>alternate</strong> (interior or exterior) angles are equal; <strong>co-interior</strong> (same-side interior) angles are supplementary, summing to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Tilt the transversal below. Every acute angle stays equal to every other acute angle (corresponding and alternate), and each is supplementary to the obtuse one.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "geoParCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Transversal angles",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
